  @contract  caller pre-pins (ppq, ppqL, rpb) onto `update` before calling  @ 852
  @contract  col nil only for a chord sprout (no column yet): no prev-vel to inherit, lane pre-set  @ 853
  @invariant  notes ordered by entry; members re-resolved via cells[row], never held event refs  @ 1200
  @contract  arms on a note col's first pitch stop; pins (row, chan) until shift release  @ 1220
  @contract  returns true iff consumed; false lets the drain fall through (to value-digit entry)  @ 1221
  @contract  re-striking a gesture pitch toggles it off; freed slots are reused lowest-first  @ 1222
  @contract  spreadChan strikes walk channels up from home; plain strikes stack home-channel lanes  @ 1223
  @invariant  pins (col,row,part); overwrites a place keep-below, steps the sub-caret right  @ 1343
  @invariant  field re-read via cells[row] each keystroke; undo snapshots drive backspace-restore  @ 1344
  @contract  target, facility and key are remembered at take tier; the rest is per invocation  @ 2243
  @contract  with no target the whole of it is the notation snap  @ 2244
  @contract  the facility reads the target as points of the pitch line or as moves between strands  @ 2245
  @contract  purity is the moves facility's alone: how nearly a spelled interval sounds pure  @ 2246
  @contract  ambient is the moves facility's alone: the share of its sonority a strand rests on  @ 2247
  @contract  returns the steps whose empty shortlists refused the solve, else nil  @ 2248
  @contract  widen stretches those windows to the nearest points instead, so none refuses  @ 2249
  @contract  selection must be exactly one grid column; multi-col selection is a no-op  @ 3047
  @invariant  a 1-col block stays contiguous when it lands on the destination col  @ 3048
  @contract  cursor follows to the destination column (single event and selection alike)  @ 3049
  @contract  refuse if dest col has any onset in source's row extent (note: note-on; else any event)  @ 3050
  @invariant  source's row extent = selection's [r1,r2] for a block, moved event's onset row for a single  @ 3051
  @invariant  tails (either direction) clipped by tm's tail pass; never block  @ 3052
  @contract  per-frame overlay for the chain the caret addresses: notes to ghost, cells to suppress  @ 3590
  @contract  the gate is fxHostAtCursor -- a cell that runs no chain of its own answers nil  @ 3591
  @contract  the window is the viewport's rows, resolved on the producer's own channel  @ 3592
  @contract  notes[colIndex][row] = tm's record by reference; note columns only; first onset wins  @ 3626
  @contract  values[colIndex][row] = { val }; the producer's claimed targets only  @ 3627
  @contract  hidden[cell] = true for every plain original this chain parked; a host cell never hides  @ 3628
  @invariant  a ghosted row may also carry a real cell; precedence is the draw arm's  @ 3629
  @invariant  the overlay lands in the columns that exist; a claim materialises none of its own  @ 3630
  @contract  reentrancy-guarded; bails on no-take (page shows placeholder)  @ 4121
  @contract  takeChanged=true resets ec and re-reads resolution/length/timeSigs  @ 4122
  @contract  grid + ctx rebuild each call; pushMute at end  @ 4123
  @contract  a column's cells/ghosts carry while its events table + projection epoch are unchanged  @ 4124
